## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to implement runtime tenant isolation in a lightweight way, showing practical use of JWT claims, middleware, IAM, and CI rollback without redesigning data stores.

## Key Concepts

- JWT tenant_id validation
- Cloud Endpoints + IAP gating
- Cloud Run service account with least privilege
- IAM Conditions to enforce per-tenant access
- CI testing with synthetic tenants and rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal example: Express middleware validates tenant_id in JWT
async function tenantMiddleware(req, res, next) {
  const tenant = req.user?.tenant_id;
  const allowed = new Set((process.env.ALLOWED_TENANTS || '').split(',').filter(Boolean));
  if (!tenant || !allowed.has(tenant)) return res.status(403).send('Forbidden');
  req.tenant = tenant;
  next();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle tenant on-boarding/off-boarding and key rotation?
- How would you monitor and alert for misconfigurations or access anomalies?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical implementation of per-tenant isolation in a shared GCP project, focusing on real-world controls rather than theory.

## Key Concepts
- IAM Conditions and least-privilege service accounts
- VPC Service Controls and Private Service Connect
- Customer-managed encryption keys (CMEK)
- CI/CD gates with synthetic tenants and rollback safety
- Data Loss Prevention (DLP) and ongoing IAM reviews

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo snippet: enforce tenant-scoped sink bindings
const sink = getSink("bigquery-export");
bindPolicy(sink, {
  condition: {
    title: "tenant_scope",
    expression: 'resource.name.startsWith("projects/PROJ/datasets/tenant-")'
  },
  bindings: [{ role: "roles/bigquery.dataEditor", members: ["serviceAccount:tenant-a-sa@proj.iam.gserviceaccount.com"] }]
});
```

